"prose": [
{
"from": 146,
"to": 149,
"text": "The boot path the chunk touches is the `escher-session` binary's served table (step 4). Its smoke is `cli_commands`, which starts each of the seven served tasks through the built binary as a process and reads its first answer; the host role serving the order page is `host_log`'s. There is no live leg: the cold-agent pipe is changed and held offline by its contract tests, never run (the live run is «Cold-agent live run»'s, F3)."
},
{
"from": 151,
"to": 153,
"text": "The diff is OS-sensitive in one case: the panic item's `file` is the path rustc records for the page, read separator-agnostically by step 5; the Test (windows) and Test (macos) jobs witness it, and the cross-OS digests of step 7, through the CI read below."
},
{
"from": 155,
"to": 165,
"text": "Controls (implement's one-shot `gate.py control`, each on the entry named, its case by name, `--timeout` sized to the case, a `timeout` reading never read as held): - (a) In `scripts/cold-agent.sh`'s `capability-unused` line, remove the `caused_by_kind` check. Entry: the cold-agent   unittest. Case `test_each_unused_capability_fails` (its `caused_by_kind` sub-cases pass with no reason, so the case   reads failed). `--timeout 120`. - (b) In `caused_by_kind`, read `\"cause\"` in place of `\"caused\"`. Same entry. Case   `test_caused_is_counted_by_kind_from_the_acting_answers`. `--timeout 120`. - (c) In `STAND_PROMPT`, delete goal 7's sentence «read what that action caused to find out why». Same entry. Case   `test_the_prompt_names_no_stand_id`. `--timeout 120`. - (d) In `tasks/order.rs`, take the `ErrorBoundary` out so the `Err` reaches the root boundary. Entry: the order page's   stand check. Case `each_control_answers_what_it_caused`, whose `boundary` `own` atom reads red. `--timeout 900`."
}
],
